The mathematical audit is complete: boundary cases (`[]`, `t−1`, `t`, `t+1`, and a later equal element) agree between the recursive summary and the operational loop/early-return semantics, and no candidate rule supplies a separate domain fact. I also verified the signed audit-input digest and the mechanical-checker lock, including every locked trusted-tool file. I’m writing the self-contained review and final pair now.
